md`### Compilation, source to runtime variable(s)

\`compile(source)\` turns a Notebook Kit JavaScript cell into runtime variable definitions. An expression, or a program with no top-level declarations, is one variable. A program declaring \`a\` and \`b\` is a holder variable \`cell <id>\` returning \`{a, b}\`, plus one projection variable per name, as in notebook-kit's \`src/runtime/define.ts\`.

Static imports become leading \`await import(…)\` lines, with specifiers kept verbatim. A cell that only imports from an Observable notebook (\`observable:@user/nb\`) compiles to lopecode's reactive import variables instead. TypeScript cells are not supported.`
