\`decompile(cells)\` returns the source. The transpiler wraps the source verbatim, so decompilation slices the wrapper off instead of generating code, and \`decompile(compile(source)) === source\` up to one leading or trailing newline. Projection variables are recognised by their shape, \`(exports) => exports["a"]\`.`
