md`## Runtime

\`defineCell(module, definition, {variables})\` defines a compiled cell's variables in a module and returns them. It creates the cell's display state and its \`display\` and \`view\` shadow variables with the variables, because \`_shadow\` cannot be added afterwards. It does not observe them. \`attachDisplay(variable, observe)\` attaches notebook-kit's observer once, however many panes call it, and returns a detach function. \`displayStateOf(variable)\` returns the state, or \`undefined\` for a variable \`defineCell\` did not create.

\`display\`, \`clear\`, \`observe\`, \`input\` and \`Mutator\` are notebook-kit 2.5.6's, loaded by \`nkRuntime\` from \`notebook-kit-runtime-2.5.6.js.gz\`. States live in \`nkDisplayStates\`, a WeakMap kept observed so a recompute does not replace it.`
